    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Speed of sound is highest in solids, moderate in liquids, lowest in gases, and strictly zero in a vacuum.",
        "To hear a clear echo, the minimum distance between the listener and reflecting surface must be 17.2 meters (with persistent hearing time of 0.1 s).",
        "Loudness depends on amplitude (Loudness ∝ Amplitude²), whereas Pitch depends directly on Frequency.",
        "Bats and dolphins use ultrasonic sound waves (frequency > 20 kHz) for navigation and prey detection via echolocation."
      ],
